ive (pairwise Jaccard 1.0, step_13) \u2014 they switch as one bloc.\n- *Comparison group:* high-activity outsiders 1714/241 show flat ~0.94\u20130.99 turnover with no localised peak (step_12), confirming the group's 0.12\u21921.0\u21920.2 profile is a genuine localised transition.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_c1b49572\",\n  \"decision\": \"present\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"regime_switch\",\n  \"entities\": [214, 315, 522, 860, 919, 1085, 1390, 1431, 1589, 1672, 1860, 1936],\n  \"window\": [2551, 32551],\n  \"confidence\": 0.93,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_16\", \"role\": \"support\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"The 12-node group abruptly replaced its entire contact set at t~16781. Before/after diff with a 5000-unit half-window yields Jaccard 0.0 (135 old edges, 96 new, no overlap), versus ~0.50-0.56 overlap for equivalent adjacent windows earlier and later in the same period, so this is a discrete switch rather than gradual churn. Unique edges drop to zero for t in [17000,18499] and resume with the new cohort, marking a sharp seam. Alternative explanations fail: there is no activ